    turnFlow: '1. **Deal**: Four cards each from a 32-card deck. 2. **Play**: Four tricks are played; players follow suit when able, otherwise discard any card. 3. **Trick winner**: Highest card of the led suit wins and leads next. 4. **Knocking**: After players pick up cards, and at any time during the hand, a player may knock to raise the stake by one life. 5. **Fold or stay**: Opponents may fold (take current loss) or continue. 6. **Hand result**: Winner of trick four avoids loss; others who stayed lose according to the raised stake. 7. **Elimination**: In Siwweschroom, players reaching seven penalty points drop out; last survivor wins.',
