    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 4 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Avoid penalty points by winning the fourth (last) trick, or by staying out of expensive losing positions after knocks.',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. **Deal**: Four cards each from a 32-card deck. 2. **Play**: Four tricks are played; players follow suit when able, otherwise discard any card. 3. **Trick winner**: Highest card of the led suit wins and leads next. 4. **Knocking**: After players pick up cards, and at any time during the hand, a player may knock to raise the stake by one life. 5. **Fold or stay**: Opponents may fold (take current loss) or continue. 6. **Hand result**: Winner of trick four avoids loss; others who stayed lose according to the raised stake. 7. **Elimination**: In Siwweschroom, players reaching seven penalty points drop out; last survivor wins.',
      'Scoring example: Penalty-life system with variable stake based on knocks. Folding concedes the current stake; staying risks a larger loss if the last trick is lost. Remain in the game after all opponents have been eliminated at seven penalty points..',
